<% content_for :title, 'Social Characteristics' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Social Characteristics' do %>
  <div class='rounded-2xl border border-slate-800/70 bg-slate-950/50 p-5 space-y-8 text-sm'>

    <p class='text-slate-400'>
      The Social Characteristics function transmits the current star system configuration to
      the generator apparatus and instructs it to assign or reassign population, government,
      law level, tech level, and starport data for all inhabited worlds in the system.
      Seed parameters supplied via the form are applied to the main world; all other bodies
      receive values computed in relation to the primary.
    </p>

    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>Government</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
            The governing structure of the main world, expressed as a Traveller government code
            (0–15). Select a value to seed the generator with a specific government type; leave
            blank to allow the generator to assign one according to standard tables.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>Law Level</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
            The legal restriction level of the main world (0–15). Higher values indicate more
            pervasive regulation of personal freedoms, weapons, and commerce. Leave blank for
            a randomly generated value.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>Population Code</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
            The population magnitude code of the main world (0–15), expressed as a hex digit
            representing an order of magnitude. A code of 7 indicates tens of millions of
            inhabitants. Leave blank for a randomly generated value.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-slate-200'>Tech Level</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-slate-300'>
            The technological sophistication of the main world (0–33). Influences the tech
            levels of subsidiary worlds in the system. Leave blank to allow the generator to
            compute an appropriate value based on the world's physical profile.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-deepnight-orange mb-4'>Operational Notes</p>

      <ul class='space-y-2 text-slate-400 list-disc list-inside'>
        <li>All seed parameters are optional. Any field left blank is assigned by the generator.</li>
        <li>Existing physical characteristics — size, atmosphere, hydrographics — are preserved.</li>
        <li>The UWP string for each inhabited world is recomputed following assignment.</li>
        <li>This operation cannot be reversed automatically; use Replace to regenerate the full system.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-slate-500'>
      REFERENCE 0402SC
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
